phis (0.4.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A Site's CDN: one bucket of files published once and served from a host
    of their own. A Storage Profile flagged Cdn (phis storage add --cdn)
    holds it; no Space writes to it and no CORS or lifecycle rule is
    written into it. New tables phis.site_cdns and phis.site_cdn_files.
  * phis cdn attach|detach|publish|list|withdraw|check|nginx|tls. publish
    uploads straight to the storage over the Provider's presigned plan, in
    parts above 16 MiB with each part's SHA-256 signed in, carries an
    interrupted upload on, and records the file. A key
    <name>/<version>/<file> is written once. HTML, SVG, XML and JavaScript
    are refused; the host serves attachment and nosniff.
  * Add-on capability @phis/server/cdn:v1: the catalogue, read-only.
  * phis storage add --create-bucket [--website]: the Provider creates its
    storage (provisionStorage). Garage gives such a bucket a key-local
    name its website does not serve; create CDN buckets there with garage.
  * phis addon migrate extends an existing Add-on schema with new tables,
    columns that may be empty or have a default, indexes and foreign keys,
    and refuses everything else with the purge advice.
  * Schema: CREATE TABLE phis.site_cdns and phis.site_cdn_files (by hand
    on existing databases).

